    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Description\n\nI'm trying to write picker that can switch between searching for files and searching for directories to then open them in mini.files. I've written custom action 'toggle' that uploads directories from fd and should redefine 'toggle' to load file items from fd. But the action is not redefined\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.3\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. write code\r\n```\r\nM.pick_dirs_action = function ()\r\n    local opts = {\r\n        mappings = {\r\n            toggle = {\r\n                char = '<c-f>',\r\n                func = M.pick_files_action,\r\n            },\r\n        },\r\n    }\r\n    MiniPick.set_picker_opts(opts)\r\n    MiniPick.set_picker_items_from_cli{ 'fd', '--type=d', '--no-follow', '--color=never' }\r\nend\r\nM.pick_files_action = function ()\r\n    local opts = {\r\n        mappings = {\r\n            toggle = {\r\n                char = '<c-f>',\r\n                func = M.pik_dirs_action,\r\n            },\r\n        },\r\n    }\r\n    MiniPick.set_picker_opts(opts)\r\n    MiniPick.set_picker_items_from_cli{ 'fd', '--type=f', '--no-follow', '--color=never' }\r\nend\r\n\r\nM.pick_files = function (local_opts, opts)\r\n    opts = vim.tbl_deep_extend(\r\n        'force',\r\n        {\r\n            mappings = {\r\n                toggle = {\r\n                    char = '<c-f>',\r\n                    func = M.pick_dirs_action,\r\n                },\r\n            },\r\n        },\r\n        opts or {}\r\n    )\r\n    MiniPick.builtin.files(local_opts, opts)\r\nend\r\nvim.keymap.set('n', '<leader>fd', M.pick_files)\r\n\r\n```\r\n \r\n3. press '<leader>fd' then <c-f><c-f>\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nAfter first <c-f> items change to directories. After second they should change back\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nItems stay as directories",
