            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> choosing the directory opens file explorer but then closes it after 1 second. I assume it's because of how picker is closed. Is there some workaround?\r\n\r\nNot really because of how picker is closed, but how 'mini.files' is opened. \r\n\r\n'mini.pick' automatically returns focus to its target window (as mentioned [here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/2faada1cffce5609d78ac5e81eaf3754e0476758/doc/mini-pick.txt#L836-L837)) but not immediately (for various reasons). In turn, 'mini.files' is autoclosed if it is not in focus (which is checked periodically every second). So it autocloses once it understands that it is not in focus.\r\n\r\nUsing `vim.schedule(function() MiniFiles.open(MiniPick.get_picker_opts().source.cwd .. '/' .. item, false) end)` should work here.",
